4. After the encryption process is complete, the program displays a message with the encryption key.
5. Finally, the program asks the user to pay the ransom to decrypt the files.

**Note:** This simulated ransomware program does not actually encrypt any files. It simply renames the files with an encrypted extension to give the illusion of encryption. This is a safe and legal way to demonstrate the functionality of a ransomware program without causing any harm to your system or data.

